 "validate": "H8",
 "narrative": "This batch separates strong robustness evidence from several near-null follow-ups. The two screen-quality robustness tests are convincing. H54 shows that MSI-high association with WRN dependency is essentially unchanged among lines with screen_roc_auc at or above the median: signed estimate about +0.790 with interval about +0.751 to +0.829. Under direction -1, this means MSI-high lines have substantially more negative WRN scores, i.e. much stronger WRN dependency, even in higher-quality screens. H55 similarly preserves the TP53-loss/USP7 association in high-quality screens, signed estimate about +0.426 with interval about +0.332 to +0.519; direction +1 means TP53-loss lines have higher USP7 scores, i.e. weaker USP7 dependency. Both are far from zero and large relative to the scale of the dependency scores, so multiplicity and ordinary sampling noise are not plausible explanations for these specific results. The remaining main-effect tests were biologically plausible but not supported: NF1 loss was not associated with stronger KRAS dependency (H49), PTEN loss was not associated with stronger EGFR dependency (H50), MYC amplification was not associated with stronger USP7 dependency (H51), CDKN2A loss was not associated with stronger KIF18A dependency (H52), and STK11 loss was not associated with stronger STAT3 dependency (H53). H60 further shows PTEN loss was not associated with stronger ERBB2 dependency. These are rejects of the directional association hypotheses in this dataset; they are not proof of exact nulls, but their point estimates are near zero and their intervals are compatible only with small contrasts that do not meet the practical-meaningfulness bar used here. The interaction tests mostly do not establish meaningful context dependence. H56 rejects positive ARID1A-loss modification of the SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2 effect; the point estimate leans slightly negative and the positive upper bound is small, so the hypothesized amplification is unsupported and closed. H57 and H59 remain unresolved but deferred: their interaction intervals are centered near zero but wide enough that modest interactions are not excluded, though current evidence does not justify acting on them. H58 rejects the hypothesized negative MYC-amplification modification of TP53-loss/USP7; the interval is wide and the point estimate is opposite the claimed direction, so it is not decisive enough to overturn the main TP53-loss result and is closed without validation. From a leakage perspective, using screen_roc_auc as an eligibility restriction is not obviously outcome leakage because it measures screen quality rather than the dependency score itself, but it is a post-screen selection variable; the accepted conclusions remain dataset-specific associations and not causal claims. Validation request: I choose H8 because MSI-high/WRN is a major accepted effect with a relatively small exposed group and has not yet received independent validation; the newly accepted high-quality-screen subset H54 strengthens it, but an independent split would be the most useful remaining confirmation.",
 "research_notes": "Round 4 appraisal update. Newly accepted robustness results: MSI-high/WRN remains huge in high screen_roc_auc screens (R43) and TP53-loss/USP7 remains large in high screen_roc_auc screens (R44). New negative/closed directional probes: NF1 loss/KRAS (R50), PTEN loss/EGFR (R51), MYC amp/USP7 (R40), CDKN2A loss/KIF18A (R41), STK11 loss/STAT3 (R42), PTEN loss/ERBB2 (R49). Interaction conclusions: ARID1A-loss does not meaningfully amplify SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2 (R45, closed); MYC amplification does not support hypothesized negative TP53-loss/USP7 interaction (R47, closed); KEAP1-loss/TP53-loss and PTEN-loss/KEAP1-loss interactions remain deferred/unresolved (R46,R48). Validation requested for H8 MSI-high/WRN due to small exposed group and lack of independent validation; scheduled or prior validations already exist for H5/H17/H14. Current accepted dataset-specific association set remains SMARCA4 loss -> stronger SMARCA2 dependency; KEAP1 loss -> weaker NFE2L2 dependency; PTEN loss -> stronger STAT3 dependency; MSI-high -> stronger WRN dependency; TP53 loss -> weaker USP7 dependency. The PTEN-loss effect appears specific relative to EGFR and ERBB2 probes. Next analysis plan: prioritize untested bypass/proliferation probes H15 and H28-H33 plus STAT3 pathway-specificity probes H46-H48; keep broad exploration balanced, but avoid validating near-nulls and avoid interpreting deferred interactions as effect modification unless evidence becomes sharper. Continue to distinguish dataset-specific association from causality/generalizability."
